{"id": "EUVD-2026-96990", "enisaUuid": "6b123b54-cf67-3460-b170-291a3dca6c6f", "description": "mcp-remote 0.8.0 through 0.14.3 contains a cleartext transmission vulnerability in authorizeWithDeviceCode that sends client secrets and receives tokens without enforcing HTTPS endpoints. When discovered device authorization and token endpoints are non-loopback http URLs, on-path network attackers can capture the client secret plus issued access and refresh tokens.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T17:01:20", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind03/punkpeye-mcp-remote-device-code-cleartext-oauth-transport", "https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/blob/v0.14.3/src/lib/device-authorization.ts#L64-L170", "https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote/blob/v0.14.3/src/lib/client-credentials.ts#L37-L47", "https://github.com/punkpeye/mcp-remote", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/mcp-remote-0.8.0-through-0.14.3-cleartext-credential-transmission-via-device-code-oauth-grant"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jrvg-vw6c-rp59", "CVE-2026-108716"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b4c5bca6-20ef-39d7-895e-70b980b9cb8c", "product": {"name": "mcp-remote", "vendor": {"name": "punkpeye"}}, "product_version": "0.8.0 \u22640.14.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bb7a762a-ae42-32b5-b1fe-3fe1dc22a7b0", "vendor": {"name": "punkpeye"}}], "isExploited": false}